POSITIVE COVERAGE
The full run projected and inspected all 38 zones, all 57 public land routes,
and all 4 public boat routes. Land classes are exactly 30 primary, 24
secondary and 3 trail. It pins numeric/id order, complete literal first,
middle and last zone and land-route records, every boat record, every zone's
primary_relief_id, the three record schemas and exact bucket rosters. It
reconstructs every relevant Source record losslessly, including false versus
real non-empty text for faction and both optional gate references. It also
proves Source immutability and absence of mutable aliases in or from output.

The complete compiled-data shell contains all 21 existing geometry families,
with the three D-1 families inserted and every other geometry family empty.
The reserved island_routes family is explicitly empty. The shell includes the
real typed selectors, spatial, coverage and release sections, and passes only
through compiled_schema.canonicalize_compiled. Its canonical bytes and the
three family arrays are hashed by the real canonical encoder/hasher.

NEGATIVE COVERAGE
The full run rejects an unknown dependency; missing and additional Source
fields; metatables; sparse arrays; mutable aliases; cycles; wrong types and
integer ranges; reordered, duplicate and changed identities; numeric and
empty-string optional gate references; land_058 boundary-only contamination;
island-route contamination; and an injected Source-validator failure before
package-local validation. A same-shape mutation is rejected by the real Source
checksum; with the explicit accepting test seam the same mutation moves the
complete-shell digest. The real canonicalizer rejects a compiled schema
identity mismatch, a negative unsigned value, unsorted named rows and a
mutable alias. Focused records plus cases remain 159, below the 300 cap.

